{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445520-v20-advice-on-how-to-use-dark-age-rules-for-modern-day","id":1445520,"title":"[V20] Advice on how to use Dark Age rules for Modern Day?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-04-23T12:45:33-07:00","id":1445520,"title":"[V20] Advice on how to use Dark Age rules for Modern Day?","content":"Long story short, I love Vampire, and have been debating on playing earlier editions or not. However, v20 itself has too many issues in my opinion, issues that were actually solved in the book line Dark Ages for v20. However, I am not familiar enough with the two editions to know how possible it would be to play Dark Ages in the modern nights. Any advice?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T13:50:05-07:00","id":1445532,"title":"","content":"I think it would be really easy, the only thing you have to port over is skills and tech. The two work well together taking from both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T14:04:23-07:00","id":1445537,"title":"","content":"The only real thing is having to update a couple of skills (Drive, Firearms, Computer/Technology). The Roads and medieval Clans work perfectly fine in the modern nights once you figure out what modern niches and tropes they fit with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T15:52:59-07:00","id":1445562,"title":"","content":"So porting things from one to the other wouldn't be too hard mechanically?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T21:00:57-07:00","id":1445597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445520-v20-advice-on-how-to-use-dark-age-rules-for-modern-day?p=1445562#post1445562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So porting things from one to the other wouldn't be too hard mechanically?</div> </div> </div> </div>The base system is pretty much identical. IIRC, the only major differences are a few of the Disciplines powers, and the use of the Roads instead of the majority of Kindred using Humanity. <br /> <br /> Probably modern firearms rules and stats for modern vehicles (and possibly drugs unless you just want to hand wave that sort of thing) are the only thing you'd have to add, I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T03:26:04-07:00","id":1445636,"title":"","content":"You should use a lot of V20 rules for disciplines. Part of this is because, although DAV20 has some very good ideas, it also took risks and has some ideas that are at least unfiting for the modern day (Obf 1, all of dementation, Serpentis 4) or downright stupid no matter the time period (quietus 1). At the least, modern thaumaturges have more paths and rituals than their DA counterparts.<br /> Of course, there are many places where DAV20 just does a lot better on the discipline front, and a lot of preference based stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T07:58:14-07:00","id":1445665,"title":"","content":"I think DAV20 Obfuscate 1 is a long overdue improvement on previous editions, and I like Serpentis 4 in DAV20. Off the top of my head fail changes in DAV20 would be Temporis level 6 where you can't actually make people older because humans would die and vampires would just drop into torpor. The first takes away a cool effect, the second is over powered. I think Obeah 5 is correct in V20, and Valeren 5 healer is incredibly game breaking in DAV20 so I would switch those two if not the powers completely. DAV20 improves celerity if I remember, just not enough and it still needs to be house ruled. I prefer DAV20 Auspex rules by a lot.<br /> <br /> Overall I agree, each one should be looked at for taste weather you switch a specific level of the discipline or the entire thing, it's very nice to have both handy.<br /> <br /> edit also Just say no to watcher salubri slide safe passage and purification back to healers, not that I have played with an ancient Salubri, I just think the watchers are like the Inconnu thread, what's the point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24221,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","user":"Vamps Like Us","date":". 04-24-2021, 11:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T02:48:10-07:00","id":1445799,"title":"","content":"I like DAV20's serpentis 4... for the dark ages and prior. The Naga form is too high fantasy for Modern nights. <br /> <br /> Obf 1 doesnt work when Obfuscate is supposed to be a mind trick. Furthermore if every Tom, dick and harry can silence gunfire with just obfuscate 1 then things get a bit sus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T04:57:26-07:00","id":1445804,"title":"","content":"It's easy, but yeah, you'll need a house rules document where you track decisions on which versions of the Disciplines you'll use. You can pick and mix, but just keep it consistent (e.g., note if you use Obfuscate 1 (V20) and Obfuscate 2-5 (V20DA)).<br /> <br /> Put something together in Google Docs and you're good to go. Some of it can be decided ahead of time and some of it while playing.<br /> <br /> I'd also use the fast combat rules in one of the V20DA supplements (Companion or Book of Secrets--I can't remember). It makes combat super lethal but also much faster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T05:08:37-07:00","id":1445806,"title":"","content":"Personally, I don't have much of a problem with a bit of High Fantasy in my Vampire. I mean, we already have vampire wizards who can run around throwing fireballs, and they're a core Clan (with the aforementioned fireballs being a core Path dating all the way back to 1st edition). That ship has already sailed.<br /> <br /> Plus, it's not as though Vicissitude's &quot;war form&quot; is any less fantastic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T06:43:01-07:00","id":1445814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445520-v20-advice-on-how-to-use-dark-age-rules-for-modern-day?p=1445799#post1445799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like DAV20's serpentis 4... for the dark ages and prior. The Naga form is too high fantasy for Modern nights.<br /> <br /> Obf 1 doesnt work when Obfuscate is supposed to be a mind trick. Furthermore if every Tom, dick and harry can silence gunfire with just obfuscate 1 then things get a bit sus.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I figured that would be the argument against Obfuscate 1, but stronger Obfuscate powers allow you to turn things invisible even after you have left, now you make things quiet to the minds of others. I chalk it up to magic. It should probably be modified to at least just follow the player around in a smaller radius though. It's only a level 1 power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T07:09:54-07:00","id":1445816,"title":"","content":"Actually maybe the description does make it clear it's a mind trick that only works in the cone of silence, if you stand a few feet out of it's range you'll hear of the fighting and gun shots, just like people inside can hear all the distant noise coming in. I still think leaving bubbles of silence is a bit much for level 1. I can see where a couple Kindred with Obfuscate could cause frustration in shutting down social gaming for laughs so I can see reasons to dislike it even if I do like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}